"""One-off: append the Eagle_Eyes 2026-10-26 live-market bugs to BUGS.md before '# END'."""
P = "MyTradingSys/research/BUGS.md"
ROWS = [
    "| B201 | 2026-10-26 | OPEN | HIGH | Operator live-market chart shots cannot be closed cheaply: `shot.py done` refuses a chart until `shot.py read --extract` has run, and `read` wants a TEMPLATE.md file (Prior line, claim rows MATCH/MISMATCH/NOT_IN_DATA with a data-check file). In live mode the operator posts a chart every few minutes and wants a bias read, not 15 claim tables, so 15 classified shots sat unclosed for hours and the intake notice kept firing. Candidate fix: a `read --live` form (one line per shot: class + bias + ladder ref, no claim rows) or let `done --outcome note:` close a chart that is already logged in a live_reads READ.md. | shot.py done REFUSED twice on 10-26 (outcome prefix, then 'chart that has not been read'); shot ids 43cec1ee0a19 c1ddfcef535f d31c5690e8c0 43fc5ddec27b 7a8737e4c81b df6257dd397a 8dc124f61332 1f3d02f3e0aa e74b902ed53e 34bad00c5501 4056ec02fa78 c9ba9cd2ca1a a3330d10c427 dbbaf63b656e 13c9d9d2cd6e | |",
    "| B202 | 2026-10-26 | OPEN | HIGH | A live watcher cannot outlive 30 minutes: the Monitor tool expires at 30 min and no scheduler is allowed, so the BTC/ES trigger watcher died 12 times in one session (re-armed each time, gaps up to about a minute, plus a stop/re-arm around each commit). Any trigger firing in a gap is lost. Candidate fix: a sanctioned long-lived local process for observation-only watchers (no orders, no live-path), started by the operator or a coordinator and listed in HOW_MTS_RUNS, or a Monitor persistent mode that survives the 30-minute cap. | watch.py armed 12x on 10-26 (10th 19:25Z, 11th ~20:00Z, 12th ~20:06Z); watch_rows.csv has the minute gaps | |",
    "| B203 | 2026-10-26 | OPEN | MED | `desk.py post --target DSA` accepts a card id that exists only as an uncommitted file in a worktree, so the DSA desk row pointed at a card no other machine could see for about 2 hours (cards lab-verify-rsi-40-60-bb-bounce-15m and lab-verify-mtf-bias-ladder). Fix: post refuses (or warns) unless `git cherry origin/fast-track` shows the card committed and shipped. | desk rows 20261026-181737-lab-verify-rsi-40-60-bollinger-boun, 20261026-200055-lab-verify-mtf-bias-ladder-higher-timefr; shipped later as CI green de501f71 | |",
    "| B204 | 2026-10-26 | OPEN | MED | Card lint rules are only discovered after the card is written, one error at a time: worker agent is allowed only for size S with est_turns <= 15, and depends_on a card that is only ready is flagged. Two cards each failed lint once and were rewritten. Fix: print all lint errors at once, and document the rules in TASK_REFINEMENT.md next to the card template. | tasks lint on timeframes-add-2d-3d-4d-5d (worker agent on size M) and lab-verify-mtf-bias-ladder (depends_on a ready card), 10-26 ~20:05Z | |",
    "| B205 | 2026-10-26 | OPEN | MED | Hook reminders for operator-run items repeat every turn and after every compaction even after the session acked `told`: b-4c2dfe, b-3ee970, b-1fdd2e, b-4053da, b-2a5b44 are things this session cannot run (primary checkout / other machine), yet each prompt carries 10 broadcast status lines plus 5 HIGH reminders. In a live-market thread this is noise that crowds out the chart. Fix: a told-with-blocker ack mutes the reminder for this host for 24 h, and the broadcast status list shows only items addressed to this host. | UserPromptSubmit / SessionStart hook output on every turn 10-26 evening | |",
    "| B206 | 2026-10-26 | OPEN | LOW | Role worktree starts stale and the hook says so on every prompt: the Eagle_Eyes worktree was 1016 commits behind origin/fast-track (58 h), and the session cannot run `git merge origin/fast-track` in it (auto-mode classifier denied the merge on 10-26 ~20:40Z; the sanctioned path is `sync.py start`, which the role session has already used). Result: STATUS.md, cards and QUICK_ANSWERS read in the worktree are 58 h old. Also the local clock is past UTC midnight (hooks print 2026-10-27 while the market log is UTC 10-26). Fix: sync.py start for a role session fast-forwards the worktree; hooks print UTC date and local date together. | TRUNK LAG hook line on every prompt; merge denied by auto mode classifier | |",
]
s = open(P, encoding="utf-8", newline="").read()
assert s.rstrip().endswith("# END"), "unexpected tail"
head, tail = s.rsplit("# END", 1)
head = head.rstrip("\n") + "\n\n"
out = head + "\n\n".join(ROWS) + "\n\n# END" + tail
open(P, "w", encoding="utf-8", newline="\n").write(out)
print("rows appended:", len(ROWS))
